From: mscharged-port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Keep a read's channel map when the head audio track ends
Upstream-base: 8e37db5e797b6167f3a00d697d816a684bd259c7

SDL_ReadFromAudioQueue takes src_map from the head track, then reads the
present frames. When that read finishes the head track, ReadFromAudioQueue
destroys it, and ConvertAudio swizzles through the freed track's chmap
storage. A stream with an input channel map that queues small NoCopy tracks
hits this whenever one read spans tracks; once the track pool is full the
block is really freed and its memory reused. Copy the map into local storage
before reading. SDL main still has the same code.

diff --git a/src/audio/SDL_audioqueue.c b/src/audio/SDL_audioqueue.c
index b59e847..780638c 100644
--- a/src/audio/SDL_audioqueue.c
+++ b/src/audio/SDL_audioqueue.c
@@ -535,7 +535,14 @@ const Uint8 *SDL_ReadFromAudioQueue(SDL_AudioQueue *queue,
 
     SDL_AudioFormat src_format = track->spec.format;
     int src_channels = track->spec.channels;
-    const int *src_map = track->chmap;
+    // Reading the present frames below can finish and destroy this head
+    // track. Keep a copy of its channel map rather than a pointer into it.
+    int src_map_storage[SDL_MAX_CHANNELMAP_CHANNELS];
+    const int *src_map = NULL;
+    if (track->chmap) {
+        SDL_memcpy(src_map_storage, track->chmap, sizeof (*track->chmap) * src_channels);
+        src_map = src_map_storage;
+    }
 
     size_t src_frame_size = SDL_AUDIO_BYTESIZE(src_format) * src_channels;
     size_t dst_frame_size = SDL_AUDIO_BYTESIZE(dst_format) * dst_channels;
